  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nLet's compare the coefficients:\n\n- The coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ on the left-hand side is $m,$ and on the right-hand side it is $6.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nm=6.\n$$\n\n- The coefficient of $x$ on the left-hand side is $n,$ and on the right-hand side it is $-3.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nn=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}mn & =6\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
